  "pr.eye":"From the catalogue","pr.h":"Manetti<br>products",
  "pr.p":"Selected items, photographed for the Manetti catalogues. Each one opens its own catalogue page, with formats, shades and codes.",
  "pr.link":"See in the catalogue",
  "p.foglia-libretto.h":"Leaf books","p.foglia-libretto.p":"Loose leaf for restoration and elaborate surfaces, oil or water gilding. Transfer leaf is pressed onto tissue paper without glue: faster on flat surfaces and always recommended outdoors. 25 leaves per book.",
  "p.libretto-singolo.h":"Retail leaf books","p.libretto-singolo.p":"A single booklet of 5 or 25 leaves in its own box, 9 shades of genuine gold, 8×8 and 8.6×8.6 cm. Real gold made easy to buy for artists, students and small workshops.",
  "p.foglia-rotolo.h":"Leaf rolls","p.foglia-rotolo.p":"Leaves laid by hand, overlapping, on a 20.5 m tissue-paper roll. Quick, precise gilding of large flat surfaces, indoors and out; a roll applicator is available.",
  "p.foglia-glass.h":"Glass leaf","p.foglia-glass.p":"Glass leaf for the verre églomisé technique: a mirror finish on glass, ready to be engraved or decorated.",
  "p.foglia-imitazione.h":"Imitation leaf","p.foglia-imitazione.p":"A copper-zinc alloy for gold, 100% aluminium for silver and pure copper. Thicker leaf that can be handled by hand, ideal for beginners and gilding schools. 14×14 cm books of 25.",
  "p.kit-cornice.h":"Kit — gilding a frame","p.kit-cornice.p":"Manetti's first starter kit for hobbyists, beginners and students: genuine 24K gold leaf, water-based size, brush, cloth, protection and a wooden frame, with a detailed step-by-step guide.",
  "p.bolo-italiano.h":"Italian bole","p.bolo-italiano.p":"Clay base for water gilding on wood primed with gesso. Yellow, red and black; diluted with a rabbit skin glue solution, the leaf is laid while it is still wet.",
  "p.missione.h":"Gold sizes","p.missione.p":"Water-based size for interiors on wood, gesso and stucco. Oil-based size for wood, metal, glass and plastic, indoors and out, in 3-hour and 12-hour versions.",
  "p.gommalacca.h":"Shellac","p.gommalacca.p":"Seals porous surfaces before sizing and gives finished gilding shine and light protection. In solution or flakes; dewaxed shellac dries more transparent.",
  "p.bitume.h":"Bitumen and wax","p.bitume.p":"Ready-to-use mixtures for patinating and ageing gilded surfaces. Water-based bitumen is not flammable and can ship by air; bituminous wax gives the much-loved antique effect.",
  "p.brunitoi.h":"Agate burnishers","p.brunitoi.p":"A wooden handle with a polished agate tip, for burnishing water gilding to a shine. Various shapes and sizes for every contour.",
  "p.cuscinetto-coltello.h":"Cushion, knife and tip","p.cuscinetto-coltello.p":"A 28×18 cm leather-topped cushion to lay out and cut the leaf; a single- or double-edged metal knife; an animal-hair gilder's tip to carry the leaf from the book to the surface.",
  "p.foglia-decalco.h":"Leaf for outdoors","p.foglia-decalco.p":"For outdoor work Manetti recommends transfer leaf in Extra thickness: more metal in the leaf means better resistance to wear and weather and a longer-lasting gild.",
  "p.protezione-esterni.h":"Exterior protection","p.protezione-esterni.p":"Acrylic topcoat for outdoor gilding with precious or imitation leaf: high resistance to yellowing and a gloss finish. Used with its catalyst.",
  "q.mat.eye":"From the Manetti catalogue","q.mat.h":"Materials<br>for the site",
  "q.mat.p":"What the Manetti catalogue recommends for façades, domes and large surfaces. Tap to open the catalogue page.",

  "g.eye":"For the kitchen","g.h":"Gold Chef",
  "g.p":"Edible gold and silver for fine dining, pastry and bars. Pure metal, no additives, no taste or scent. The European Union allows its use as colouring: E175 for gold, E174 for silver.",
  "g.f1":"Leaf","g.f1p":"A whole 86 × 86 mm sheet. For wrapping and larger surfaces.",
  "g.f2":"Flakes","g.f2p":"Irregular petals. A living, torn shimmer on desserts and in cocktails.",
  "g.f3":"Crumbs","g.f3p":"A fine fraction. An even scatter across the plate, taken by the pinch.",
  "g.f4":"Powder","g.f4p":"The finest dusting. A continuous coat on mousses and drinks.",
  "g.useh":"How to apply it","g.us1h":"Open the booklet","g.us1p":"The leaf rests between sheets of tissue. Work away from draughts: the leaf is lighter than air.",
  "g.us2h":"Lift it with tweezers","g.us2p":"Dry tweezers or a brush. Never touch the gold with your fingers, it will stick to the skin.",
  "g.us3h":"Place it on the dish","g.us3p":"At the very last moment before serving, onto a dry or slightly damp surface.",
  "g.note":"The Gold Chef, Luxury and Industrial series are available. Packs of 0.07 g, 0.125 g, 0.2 g, 1 g, 3 g, 10 g, in gold and silver.",

  "a.eye":"Gilding Academy","a.h":"The school<br>of gilding",
  "a.p":"Gilding is a trade learned with the hands. Gathered here is what the Manetti craftsmen pass to their apprentices: which techniques exist, how they differ, and when each one is the right one.",
  "a.t1h":"Water gilding","a.t1p":"The classic water-based technique: gesso, bole, water. It gives a mirror surface that can be burnished with agate. For frames, icons and carving.",
  "a.t2h":"Mordant gilding","a.t2p":"The leaf is laid on an oil or water mordant. Easier to work, more resistant to damp, not burnished. For interiors, facades and signs.",
  "a.t3h":"Patina and ageing","a.t3p":"Finished gilding can be aged, toned and given depth. It has its own set of preparations and methods.",
  "a.t4h":"Protecting the surface","a.t4p":"Varnishes and protective coatings for areas under load, outdoor work and surfaces that hands touch.",
  "a.ask":"Need advice on a technique, or the right materials for a particular job? Write to us and we will talk it through.",

